## Runtime notes for the assessor

* fapolicyd runs deny-by-default. Non-RPM runtime binaries are in
  /etc/fapolicyd/trust.d/kubernetes and /etc/fapolicyd/rules.d/35-kubernetes.rules
  allows CNI plugins installed into /opt/cni/bin at runtime.
  /etc/fapolicyd/rules.d/25-runc.rules lets runc's sealed self re-exec
  (subject `/runc`, which fapolicyd classifies as the ld_so pattern) open the
  dynamic linker cache and its shared libraries; without it no container can
  start. It allows opens only, for that subject only; running ld.so directly
  on an untrusted binary is still denied.
* CNI plugins may change networking sysctls (e.g. per-interface rp_filter) on
  a running node.
* The Kubernetes STIG covers the cluster (API server, kubelet configuration,
  etc.). It is applied by the platform at cluster creation, not by this image.
